    "function": {
        "name": "get_weather",
        "description": "Get the current weather for a city.",
        "parameters": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {"city": {"type": "string"}},
            "required": ["city"],
        },
    },
}]
​
response = client.chat.completions.create(
    model="accounts/fireworks/models/muse-spark-open",
    messages=[{"role": "user", "content": "What's the weather in Menlo Park?"}],
    tools=tools,
)
print(response.choices[0].message.tool_calls)
Streaming (stream=True) and JSON mode (response_format={"type": "json_object"}) work the same way they do for other Fireworks chat models.

More
Serverless is billed per token for input, cached input, and output. Current rates are on the 
model page
.
Prompt caching is automatic. Repeated prefixes, such as long system prompts and agent histories, are billed at the cached-input rate.
For dedicated GPUs, higher rate limits, or reserved throughput, create an 
on-demand deployment
 of the same model, or 
contact Fireworks
.
Fireworks also serves an 
Anthropic-compatible Messages API
, so Muse Spark Open can run in coding agents built for that API.
